                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2ae222b0-2629-4626-ac75-21b7d4fba578",
                        "source_entry_id": "ce329157-80d0-3c98-a39f-a19955c97835",
                        "source_sense_id": "10d8f5d6-59e9-3d0f-86b5-b84125036d3c",
                        "target_lang_word": "epidemic",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "epidemic",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b774907b-502f-3cfa-97f8-7ed6f5abfc68",
                                        "entry_id": "4f44152b-fe10-383a-92f9-a23342acf747",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A widespread disease that affects many humans in a population."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c3bee367-d59b-4f8f-8954-402652391eb5",
                                                "sense_id": "b774907b-502f-3cfa-97f8-7ed6f5abfc68",
                                                "text": "At that time, the city [Christiania, now Oslo] was in the grip of a cholera epidemic, and victims were dying at the rate of 60 a day. Bradshaw contracted the disease, and died on September 6 [1853]."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b2c49c7f-ca83-3bdd-94c9-f42625c89c69",
                                        "entry_id": "4f44152b-fe10-383a-92f9-a23342acf747",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An occurrence of a disease or disorder in a human population at a frequency higher than that expected in a given time period; an episode of outbreak and subsequent high prevalence."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5ffaa791-a50d-33c7-8ec7-72fc7f47c229",
                                        "entry_id": "4f44152b-fe10-383a-92f9-a23342acf747",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A heightened occurrence of anything harmful."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly",
                                            "colloquial"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d9086b9c-2cfc-46b9-90d8-386f0a275ba0",
                                                "sense_id": "5ffaa791-a50d-33c7-8ec7-72fc7f47c229",
                                                "text": "Even before the pandemic, the United States surgeon general, Vivek Murthy, said the country was experiencing an “epidemic of loneliness,” driven by the accelerated pace of life and the spread of technology into all of our social interactions."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a61f3b1d-8bd7-4859-8653-32734a226b36",
                                                "sense_id": "5ffaa791-a50d-33c7-8ec7-72fc7f47c229",
                                                "text": "People are holding coordinated protests across UK towns and cities this weekend against what they call a “climate of fear” on the roads, and an “epidemic” of careless and dangerous driving that is curbing children’s freedoms and putting lives at risk."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f3ef3ca8-d3c3-3819-8983-de8e7cedc30a",
                                        "entry_id": "4f44152b-fe10-383a-92f9-a23342acf747",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The spreading of an idea or belief amongst a population."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d9a502f4-8667-43e6-a956-bbb0a5fb757b",
                                                "sense_id": "f3ef3ca8-d3c3-3819-8983-de8e7cedc30a",
                                                "text": "Lord Avonleigh was at once liberated from his imprisonment, well prepared to be considered, and to consider himself, a martyr to the cause of loyalty; and as the services of the rich nobleman,...his claims to notice and favour were most graciously acknowledged. Accordingly, he returned to his seat in a little fever of royal devotedness—it was the fashionable epidemic; and who coming from Whitehall could be without it?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "epidemic",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "29dacaf7-3b19-3f4f-84d2-11deb0675605",
                                        "entry_id": "28ce6a1e-7d31-39c1-aa91-6010cca33d11",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of, related to, or being an epidemic: a widespread outbreak of disease in humans."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6f01755a-c4a3-389d-ae76-91b5e57e22df",
                                        "entry_id": "28ce6a1e-7d31-39c1-aa91-6010cca33d11",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Like an epidemic: widespread in a bad way."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6f2b54ad-64a2-488d-b0d0-0b918ae074fb",
                                                "sense_id": "6f01755a-c4a3-389d-ae76-91b5e57e22df",
                                                "text": "Epidemic hysteria occurred upon the incumbent’s reelection."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "25cb6fc6-a6c7-488b-be69-e93f0e87eb32",
                                                "sense_id": "6f01755a-c4a3-389d-ae76-91b5e57e22df",
                                                "text": "[In] May, there was, at London and in its neighbourhood, a disease very epidemic, though not fatal, which had some time before been very prevalent both in Italy and Germany."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7d57423b-be3b-4ddf-9360-b9f401f52a79",
                                                "sense_id": "6f01755a-c4a3-389d-ae76-91b5e57e22df",
                                                "text": "The major reason for such an examination was to determine if any patterns uncovered seemed to be more epidemic than endemic."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0c094fe2-55c6-4711-be6c-be3dc8a86128",
                                                "sense_id": "6f01755a-c4a3-389d-ae76-91b5e57e22df",
                                                "text": "This proportion increased about 5% from 1988 to 1992—hardly a change of epidemic proportions."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c88bd35f-bb2c-4219-81b3-5796591b602a",
                                                "sense_id": "6f01755a-c4a3-389d-ae76-91b5e57e22df",
                                                "text": "This was the stagecoach holdup, and while these encounters were not as epidemic as we like to remember, nonetheless there were numerous bands of \"road agents\" who lay by the roadside in wait for passengers."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6e1fac89-d6dd-4914-9d14-3dd8fd66ce09",
                        "source_entry_id": "ce329157-80d0-3c98-a39f-a19955c97835",
                        "source_sense_id": "10d8f5d6-59e9-3d0f-86b5-b84125036d3c",
                        "target_lang_word": "epidemical",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "epidemical",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ffcdcc76-3457-3968-bf26-baf465baa033",
                                        "entry_id": "a91745d3-738f-364f-9d12-28468c962814",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative form of epidemic."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "alternative",
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "27194998-b533-46d1-b597-d7d63fc9b442",
                                                "sense_id": "ffcdcc76-3457-3968-bf26-baf465baa033",
                                                "text": "Amongst other diseases the Leprosie was one epidemicall infection which tainted the Pilgrimes coming thither."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3691dc96-762e-44ca-9676-765cb357aa03",
                                                "sense_id": "ffcdcc76-3457-3968-bf26-baf465baa033",
                                                "text": "It was the epidemical sin of the nation."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "66ca78d2-36f5-480d-801b-4a2364ef1779",
                        "source_entry_id": "ce329157-80d0-3c98-a39f-a19955c97835",
                        "source_sense_id": "10d8f5d6-59e9-3d0f-86b5-b84125036d3c",
                        "target_lang_word": "épidémique",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "épidémique",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "410ecea9-c7b7-399d-8861-59fbf21125c9",
                                        "entry_id": "e2185466-d21a-31c0-8cdc-841a32f81452",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Qui tient de l’épidémie."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "63222e89-5241-4879-b132-9f1129363a36",
                                                "sense_id": "410ecea9-c7b7-399d-8861-59fbf21125c9",
                                                "text": "Après une période de six années de disette et de souffrances, une maladie épidémique, appelée peste blanche, se déclare dans la paroisse vers le mois de Mai et en décime la population. Les registres de cette année 1779 constatent 277 décès."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "73167eab-e41d-4a53-9c37-922e90fd5600",
                                                "sense_id": "410ecea9-c7b7-399d-8861-59fbf21125c9",
                                                "text": "C'est une espèce de maladie épidémique qui a régné à Paris depuis l'hiver dernier. Il y en a beaucoup aux filles Sainte-Marie de la rue du Bac et plusieurs en sont mortes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9dbd6dc4-c343-4da6-8048-9be3dfd61375",
                                                "sense_id": "410ecea9-c7b7-399d-8861-59fbf21125c9",
                                                "text": "Ainsi, depuis une semaine, et la décision prise par Jean-Michel Blanquer de ne pas reculer la rentrée de janvier malgré la flambée épidémique, l’école de la République ressemble de plus en plus à une énorme centrifugeuse à virus et de moins en moins à une machine à instruire."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "06280616-0fba-36c5-9f0c-598865c58aef",
                                        "entry_id": "e2185466-d21a-31c0-8cdc-841a32f81452",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Qui se répand rapidement, parmi un grand nombre de gens."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "analogy",
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "10b1f533-4980-4aa7-8d63-cfd697c20990",
                                                "sense_id": "06280616-0fba-36c5-9f0c-598865c58aef",
                                                "text": "Avec le confinement et son télétravail corollaire s’est développée une horizontalisation massive des pratiques professionnelles. Par « horizontal », il ne faut pas entendre ici une fin soudaine de toute verticalité dans les processus de décision, mais une tendance épidémique à travailler en position couchée, sur son lit ou son canapé."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "8120015a-afc3-41ae-be74-0542be788cd2",
                        "source_entry_id": "ce329157-80d0-3c98-a39f-a19955c97835",
                        "source_sense_id": "10d8f5d6-59e9-3d0f-86b5-b84125036d3c",
